# Line-ending policy
#
# Why this file exists:
# - The BP manifest integrity hash (`packages/best-practices/src/integrity.ts`)
#   reads YAML file bytes raw and feeds them into SHA-256. Git on Windows
#   defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites LF → CRLF on checkout
#   and breaks the hash — the Windows CI matrix surfaced this the first
#   time it actually dispatched (Epic 76-it2 fix), see
#   `__tests__/manifest-freshness.test.ts` on 2026-04-20 run 24668814167.
# - Without an explicit policy, deterministic artefacts (manifest hashes,
#   snapshot tests, lint formatters) drift between platforms with no
#   obvious culprit.
#
# Policy:
# - Force LF on every hash-sensitive or content-deterministic file type so
#   all platforms see the same bytes.
# - Force LF on every typical source/doc file for predictability. Windows
#   developers should set `git config --global core.autocrlf input` (the
#   standard non-macOS/non-Linux setting) — that combines with this file
#   to give clean checkouts everywhere.
# - Binary assets (images, fonts, lockfile caches) are marked binary so
#   git never touches them.

# Default: treat everything as text with auto-detected LF-normalized storage.
# This keeps git smart about new file types while keeping stored blobs clean.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Hash-sensitive / determinism-critical: explicitly LF everywhere
*.yaml       text eol=lf
*.yml        text eol=lf
*.json       text eol=lf
*.jsonl      text eol=lf
*.ts         text eol=lf
*.tsx        text eol=lf
*.js         text eol=lf
*.mjs        text eol=lf
*.cjs        text eol=lf
*.md         text eol=lf
*.mdx        text eol=lf
*.sh         text eol=lf
*.env        text eol=lf

# Shell scripts and hooks: must stay LF for POSIX interpreters
.husky/*     text eol=lf
*.bash       text eol=lf
*.zsh        text eol=lf
*.fish       text eol=lf

# Binary assets: leave git alone
*.png        binary
*.jpg        binary
*.jpeg       binary
*.gif        binary
*.webp       binary
*.ico        binary
*.pdf        binary
*.woff       binary
*.woff2      binary
